                    ^"Glory" "-3"
                }

                EFFECT {
                    "Choose one of the starting skills for your school in which your character has no ranks; gain +1 rank in that skill"
                }
            }

            6 #4Ur9bjb2KL8cCmXcYAChv4 ^"Blade of 10,000 Battles" DEF {

                MODIFIERS {
                    ^"Glory" "+3"
                }

                EFFECT {
                    "Choose a weapon and add it to your starting outfit. At the GM's discretion, certain weapons may be inappropriate choices and cannot be selected."
                    "In addition to being a weapon, this item is a battlefield heirloom (see page 90)."
                }
            }

            7 #MGZl7UIrPFoKcDf5AI1foe ^"Lost Heirloom" DEF {

                MODIFIERS {
                    ^"Honor" "+5"
                    ^"Glory" "-3"
                }

                EFFECT {
                    "Choose a weapon to be the lost heirloom, which is now held by some individual or group hostile to you or your clan. At the GM's discretion, certain weapons may be inappropriate choices and cannot be selected."
                    "In addition to being a weapon, this item is a battlefield heirloom (see page 90)."
                }
            }

            8 #FSTRVOZDQHw7x7NkI1UEoL ^"Selfless Sentinel" DEF {

                MODIFIERS {
                    ^"Honor" "+5"
                    ^"Glory" "-3"
                }

                EFFECT {
                    "Gain the Traditional Adherent (Earth) distinction"
                }
            }

            9 #vqXA6ao42WwxQ7K78n1ozk ^"Mighty Conqueror" DEF {

                MODIFIERS {
                    ^"Glory" "+3"
                    ^"Honor" "-3"
                }

                EFFECT {
                    "Choose one: double your starting koku, add one item of rarity 6 or lower to your starting items that is a battlefield heirloom (see page 90) in addition to its other properties, or gain the Glorious Deeds passion (see page 83)."
                }
            }

            10 #OXecHLPnQEYf96GmYWNcdY ^"Right Hand of the Emperor" DEF {

                MODIFIERS {
                    ^"Status" "+3"
                }

                EFFECT {
                    "Gain the Support of [One Group] distinction"
                    "The group chosen must be the Seppun, Otomo, or Miya family, or the Imperial Legions"
                }
            }
        }

        RULES {
            #E1g2D1tJ4VTUj9og4YrkUh: new_samurai_heritages "New Samurai Heritages: A variety of unique heritages arise from having a bloodline derived—at least in part—from the Lion. This is true even for non-Lion characters, who may bear Lion blood because of the marriages of members of that clan into their family lineage. Some heritages are also appropriate to the great warriors and generals of all clans, even if they are most common within the Lion.\n\nTable 2–1: New Samurai Heritages represents these backgrounds when players create a new samurai PC who has ancestral connections to the Lion Clan or to famous masters of the battlefield. This table can be used instead of Table 2–1: Samurai Heritages on page 96 of the core rulebook and should be employed in the same manner."
            #hHF2QUexSEcGUoCtsTQRYK: heritage_born_on_the_battlefield "Born on the Battlefield: One of your ancestors was born amid war and bloodshed, even if not literally on the front lines. The omens of your birth reflect an affinity for that ancestor, as such omens have done for others in your family line."
            #gWbXwrJeaLDWfafMz6iaLZ: heritage_strategic_mastermind "Strategic Mastermind: You are descended from a warrior known for their cunning and wartime acumen."
            #tVNfkkRgwEEHkgWSkhpPtF: heritage_victory_against_the_crane "Victory against the Crane: In your family, one of your ancestors held a decisive victory over the Crane. It may have been a battle, a game of shōgi, a duel, or any number of other things. The circumstances are irrelevant; the Crane were humbled, and your ancestor brought honor to your clan."
            #s2mCEHI9uvsZOmg7rxWODq: heritage_victory_against_invaders "Victory against Invaders: The Lion Clan's foremost duty is to protect the Empire from outside threats, and one of your kin acquitted themselves honorably in this endeavor long ago."
            #y9baYZm1927ZVW4Nu8ND2B: heritage_shamed_by_defeat "Shamed by Defeat: Among your kin is one who failed the clan. Whether they were beaten in battle or a duel, humiliated in court, or something else, the need to redeem your line burns within you and drives you to excel."
            #NmCYXDQjLU0twXjc2y9l5y: heritage_blade_of_10000_battles "Blade of 10,000 Battles: You have been entrusted with a storied weapon with an ancient history and lineage, and you must prove yourself worthy to continue its legacy."
            #vJSb2ioGtJAQZVlRxR12DO: heritage_lost_heirloom "Lost Heirloom: An ancestor of yours was once entrusted with a peerless weapon, but through their own failure, they lost it. It may have been taken by another clan as a trophy in battle after your ancestor's defeat, stolen by bandits or shinobi, or even dishonorably sold to cover gambling debts. Whatever its fate, it has fallen to you to recover it."
            #JdzihQIoqNorhpyJuzZNF6: heritage_selfless_sentinel "Selfless Sentinel: Your ancestor was not wellknown or highly favored, but they served with honor, if not glory, and protected Lion lands from attack for all their life."
            #Dq3VoRIusNo7FSysXgJTgL: heritage_mighty_conqueror "Mighty Conqueror: One of your ancestors once seized a valuable prize for the Lion Clan in a past war, such as a village, castle, or valuable hostage. The benefits of this prize still come to those of their descent."
            #qE30w5EiCO7sr8lzsqch6N: heritage_right_hand_of_the_emperor "Right Hand of the Emperor: The crowning glory of your line is the victory one of your ancestors won in the name of a past Emperor. They may have crushed an enemy of the Empire, won great political favor, or even been a close associate or friend of the Emperor in times past. As such, the Imperial families have more respect for you than for most clan samurai—and they expect you to achieve accomplishments as glorious as those of your ancestor."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # WEAPONS
    # ===========================

    # source (page 88)
    #tZakQXgq0Rq7FAlcwbEhym ^"Fields of Victory Weapons" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]

        ENTRIES {
            #w1htlH9boXZ1uov2uUhwWA ^"Ichiro Sapper Ax" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Axe"
                ^"Skill" STRING "Martial Arts [Melee]"
                ^"Range" STRING "1"
                ^"Damage" INTEGER 3
                ^"Deadliness" INTEGER 4
                ^"Grips" STRING "1-hand:–\n\n1-hand (Blunt): Damage +2, Deadliness –3"
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Durable"]
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 2
                ^"Cost" STRING "3 koku"
                ^"Special" STRING "An Ichirō sapper ax counts as an ax when wielded with its standard 1-hand profile, and as a blunt weapon when wielded with its blunt profile."
            }

            #wrOO9VMfx0T2vhLuTuDiBr ^"Magari Yari" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Polearm"
                ^"Skill" STRING "Martial Arts [Melee]"
                ^"Range" STRING "2"
                ^"Damage" INTEGER 7
                ^"Deadliness" INTEGER 4
                ^"Grips" STRING "2-hand: -"
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Cumbersome", "Razor-Edged", "Wargear"]
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 6
                ^"Cost" STRING "20 koku"
                ^"Special" STRING "After performing an Attack action check with a magari yari, a character suffers the Disoriented condition unless they choose to receive 3 fatigue."
            }

            #yuly6JBNnIQSqZoyERiU8B ^"Nagae Yari" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Polearm"
                ^"Skill" STRING "Martial Arts [Melee]"
                ^"Range" STRING "2"
                ^"Damage" INTEGER 5
                ^"Deadliness" INTEGER 2
                ^"Grips" STRING "2-hand: -"
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Wargear"]
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 2
                ^"Cost" STRING "1 koku"
                ^"Special" STRING "Before performing an Attack action check using a nagae yari, a character may choose to suffer the Immobilized condition. If they do and succeed on the check, they add 2 bonus successes"
            }

            #g6km3hE8vPVpZvOoIq2MOd ^"Nagamaki" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Polearm"
                ^"Skill" STRING "Martial Arts [Melee]"
                ^"Range" STRING "1-2"
                ^"Damage" INTEGER 3
                ^"Deadliness" INTEGER 5
                ^"Grips" STRING "1-hand: Cumbersome\n\n2-hand: Damage +2, Deadliness +2"
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Razor-Edged", "Wargear"]
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 4
                ^"Cost" STRING "30 koku"
            }

            #zzIgjdcDwsfrJQh0zVHyjX ^"Yoroi-Doshi" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Hand Weapon"
                ^"Skill" STRING "Martial Arts [Melee]"
                ^"Range" STRING "0"
                ^"Damage" INTEGER 2
                ^"Deadliness" INTEGER 4
                ^"Grips" STRING "1-hand: -; 2-hand: Deadliness +3"
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Concealable", "Razor-Edged", "Wargear"]
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 5
                ^"Cost" STRING "10 koku"
                ^"Special" STRING "When performing an Attack action check with a yoroi-doshi, a character may spend (op) as follows: (op): Your target treats their physical resistance as 2 lower. This effect persists until the end of your next turn."
            }
        }

        RULES {
            #L5RFV32dE3fG5hI7jK9lM1n: weapons "Weapons: Fighting for the Empire and for honor demands armaments, and the Lion call upon smiths from their lands and beyond to fill this need. While most of the clan's bushi wield katana, some of which have been passed down through generations, others employ different weapons. This especially holds true for the vast legions of ashigaru and conscripted peasants who make up the bulk of most Lion armies."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # YAJIRI (SPECIALIZED ARROWHEADS)
    # ===========================

    # source (page 89)
    #FR0YymLsWQ7r4fFkrzOoTf ^"Fields of Victory Yajiri" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]

        ENTRIES {
            #xRmXrELYQwbVtS8A4ebvdO ^"Steel-Tip Yajiri" DEF {
                ^"Effect" STRING "Adds Razor-Edged quality"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 3
                ^"Cost" STRING "1 koku each"
            }

            #PXsFI25szgH9Rnqd28vSVI ^"Jade Inlay Yajiri" DEF {
                ^"Effect" STRING "Adds Sacred quality"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 8
                ^"Cost" STRING "1 koku each"
            }

            #8snc4hO7M2Mr7pJE3JLNlE ^"Obsidian Splinter Yajiri" DEF {
                ^"Effect" STRING "+4 deadliness, Forbidden, Razor-Edged and Unholy qualities"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 9
                ^"Cost" STRING "10 koku each"
            }
        }

        RULES {
            #L5RFV33oP4qR6sT8uV0wX2y: yajiri "Yajiri (Specialized Arrowheads): As varied and unique as the artisans who craft them, yajiri are ornate steel arrowheads. These artisans favor the traditional inverted heart shape for its ability to pierce armor and hide. Many yajiri crafters engrave sacred or accusatory patterns into their arrowheads, along with ornate mon or personal sigils—either their own or those of the intended wielders. Others split the arrowhead points into two- or three-headed tips or add additional flourishes to make wielders' shots especially deadly. While many favor steel yajiri, others craft arrowheads of copper, iron, jade, or even obsidian.\n\nWhen used with a bow, these arrows modify the weapon's profile as follows:"
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # PERSONAL EFFECTS
    # ===========================

    # source (page 90)
    #sZgDyRDBvtFnGSNXqL8zip ^"Fields of Victory Personal Effects" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]

        ENTRIES {
            #Rg7XNGL2WoANdNHOm5591v ^"Animal Helm" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Personal Effect"
                ^"Cost" STRING "1 koku"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 5
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Wargear"]
                ^"Effect" STRING "When a character who wears an animal helm while leading an army or cohort in a mass battle is removed via the Cut Off the Head strategic objective, reduce the panic the cohort receives by half (rounding up)."
            }

            #1GAsSS1sXIx0olcThNdvMT ^"Blasting Powder (1 Charge)" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Personal Effect"
                ^"Cost" STRING "20 koku"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 9
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Ceremonial", "Forbidden to non-shugenja"]
                ^"Effect" STRING "If a charge of blasting powder is ignited by a stray spark, the charge explodes and each character at range 0-2 suffers 10 physical damage, items at range 0-2 gain the Damaged quality, and each character at range 0-4 suffers the Disoriented condition."
            }

            #60eX3swKV7Xky3dSwQL5FF ^"Battlefield Heirloom" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Personal Effect"
                ^"Cost" STRING "Unique (cannot be purchased)"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 0
                ^"Effect" STRING "Once per game session, a character with a battlefield heirloom may reflect on the item as a Support action. If they do, they increase their composure (and their army's discipline, during a mass battle) by 2 until the end of the scene."
            }

            #MyoLCpQp5zl7dPNhrMKo6x ^"Battlefield Medical Pack" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Personal Effect"
                ^"Cost" STRING "2 bu"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 3
                ^"Effect" STRING "Once per scene as a Support action, a character with a battlefield medical pack may remove the Bleeding condition from another character at range 0-1."
            }

            #ZT9ofw3fGExgoNmKSMQsm5 ^"Brilliant Flare" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Personal Effect"
                ^"Cost" STRING "1 koku"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 6
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Wargear"]
                ^"Effect" STRING "As a Support action, a character may make a TN 3 Martial Arts (Ranged) check to fire a flare. The flare is generally visible to all characters at range 0-6."
            }

            #mf6irWjXZfMdVEnpI7RKqf ^"Gunbai" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Personal Effect"
                ^"Cost" STRING "3 koku"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 4
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Ceremonial", "Wargear"]
                ^"Effect" STRING "A gunbai can be wielded as a one-handed Martial Arts [Melee] weapon with the following profile: Range 1, Damage 2, Deadliness 2.\n\nDuring a skirmish, a character with a gunbai readied can perform shūji targeting characters who can see them at range 0–6 (as opposed to the usual auditory range restriction of range 0–4).\n\nDuring a mass battle, for each of an army's leaders equipped with a gunbai, the army increases its discipline by 2."
            }

            #ISjHcL6cDLxgiIImMo1nBE ^"Mempo" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Personal Effect"
                ^"Cost" STRING "5 koku"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 4
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Ceremonial", "Wargear"]
            }

            #9wzMby71gHfLEIFoRbII0i ^"Saihai" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Personal Effect"
                ^"Cost" STRING "4 bu"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 3
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Ceremonial", "Wargear"]
                ^"Effect" STRING "During a mass battle, if an army's commander carries a saihai, increase the army's discipline by 2."
            }

            #5sLqKKdHbykJePFFGaMF7s ^"Sashimono" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Personal Effect"
                ^"Cost" STRING "6 bu"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 2
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Wargear"]
            }

            #m6bYRCAMze33gp1LIo8uZT ^"Smoking Pipe" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Personal Effect"
                ^"Cost" STRING "1 bu"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 2
            }

            #x17yiSLYomkBWIs1TQHJhh ^"Tetsubishi" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Personal Effect"
                ^"Cost" STRING "5 bu per handful"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 4
                ^"Effect" STRING "As an Attack and Support action, a character may scatter a handful of tetsubishi targeting a patch of ground at range 0–2. The terrain at range 0–1 from the point of impact gains the Dangerous and Ensnaring terrain quality"
            }

            #joLLVTlasZ8xob6UmKdn2i ^"Uma-Jirushi" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Personal Effect"
                ^"Cost" STRING "3 koku"
                ^"Rarity" INTEGER 7
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Resplendent", "Wargear"]
                ^"Effect" STRING "When making a Command check, a leader in a mass battle who displays a personal uma-jirushi adds one kept (ring) set to (op). Should the bearer of an uma-jirushi be killed via the Cut Off the Head or Challenge action, their army receives 4 additional panic."
            }
        }

        RULES {
            #L5RFV34zA5bC7dE9fG1hI3j: personal_effects "Personal Effects: Soldiers in wartime must equip themselves both for the battlefield and for respite afterward. To successfully navigate the chaos of war, warriors must bring the right tools."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # BLESSED TREASURES (NEMURANAI)
    # ===========================

    # source (page 92)
    #gwF6Af0yoZcx731Xe6cbSq ^"Fields of Victory Blessed Treasures" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]

        ENTRIES {
            #UAm9J9XxFwwamoOzHImAXI ^"Banner of Amaterasu" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Nemuranai"
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Durable", "Sacred"]
                ^"Effect" STRING "A character wielding this banner adds a kept (ring) set to an (op) result when making Command checks."
                ^"Quirk" STRING "While the banner is exposed to direct sunlight, all friendly forces hear battlefield orders in the voice of their first martial instructor."
                ^"Sealed Invocation" STRING "The banner has the Courage of Seven Thunders invocation within it, which the wielder may perform once per session using the Command skill instead of Theology."
            }

            #FDQfjeMS9u9dKlg6k5F4cz ^"Claws of the Kitsu" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Nemuranai"
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Durable", "Sacred"]
                ^"Quirk" STRING "While carried in a pouch or wrapped cloth, a claw struggles as if trying to escape."
                ^"Sealed Invocation" STRING "Each Claw of the Kitsu has the Vapor of Nightmares invocation within it, which the wielder may perform once per session using the Courtesy skill instead of Theology."
            }

            #nPmjX7ZLUo7afyVTwSTe40 ^"Five Akodo Daggers" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Nemuranai"
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Durable", "Sacred"]
                ^"Effect" STRING "These knives have +2 deadliness."
                ^"Quirk" STRING "The Akodo Daggers grow uncomfortably hot if the blades of two or more of them come into contact with each other."
                ^"Sealed Invocation" STRING "Each dagger has the Biting Steel invocation sealed within it, which the wielder may perform once per session using the Martial Arts [Melee] skill instead of Theology."
            }

            #zqTRe1zi6d3d7wpWBaILXp ^"Leadership Scrolls" DEF {
                ^"Category" STRING "Blessed Treasure"
                ^"Qualities" LIST OF STRING ["Durable", "Sacred"]
                ^"Effect" STRING "As a support action, a character may spend one Void point and read from the scroll. If they do, they may use the Tactics skill instead of the skill they would normally use when making Social skill checks. This effect persists until the end of the scene."
            }
        }

        RULES {
            #L5RFV35kL6mN8oP0qR2sT4u: blessed_treasures "Blessed Treasures: The following blessed treasures pertain to Rokugan's glorious history of warfare, and as can be imagined, many are tied to the Lion Clan. Many are nemuranai, or awakened items (see page 307 of the core rulebook). All are rare and hard to acquire; GMs may wish to require characters to engage in long quests to locate or prove themselves worthy of such items."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # ITEM PATTERNS
    # ===========================

    # source (page 93)
    #Gm540Wnfgz6uEr2Rk0N3Nn ^"Fields of Victory Item Patterns" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]

        ENTRIES {
            #yf3n7gU30f1XO6jOu2FvSr ^"Akodo Pattern" DEF {
                ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 6
                ^"Rarity Modifier" STRING "+4"
                ^"Applies To" STRING "Weapon or armor"
                ^"Effect" STRING "A character carrying or wearing one or more items made in the Akodo pattern increases the discipline of any army of which they are the commander by 5."
            }

            #aknX7aL2m7dOytvzBZ6sdB ^"Burning Water Pattern" DEF {
                ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 6
                ^"Rarity Modifier" STRING "+4"
                ^"Applies To" STRING "Blasting powder"
                ^"Effect" STRING "Blasting powder fashioned using the burning water pattern has its damage reduced by 1. Blasting powder fashioned using the burning water pattern can be used when wet or even underwater."
            }

            #eIkNggjKy3iuK9PD7aSIAS ^"Concealment Pattern" DEF {
                ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 6
                ^"Rarity Modifier" STRING "+4"
                ^"Applies To" STRING "Armor"
                ^"Effect" STRING "Armor produced with the concealment pattern gains the Wargear quality, and loses the Ceremonial and Resplendent qualities; it cannot gain those qualities. Reduce its supernatural resistance by 1 (to a minimum of 0). While a character wearing it is in Obscuring terrain, they increase the TN of Attack action checks targeting them by an additional 1 (to a total of +2)."
            }

            #8DX5e6Spj3OZguNQ6Stwhj ^"Deadly Fangs Pattern" DEF {
                ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 7
                ^"Rarity Modifier" STRING "+4"
                ^"Applies To" STRING "Polearm"
                ^"Effect" STRING "A polearm made in the deadly fangs pattern gains the Cumbersome quality and increases its deadliness by 1. If an entire cohort is equipped with polearms with the deadly fangs pattern, its leader reduces the TN of the Reinforce action by 1 (to a minimum of 1)."
            }

            #QZ2UA0k5tsqxs4xsOhJTO0 ^"Fearsome Snarl Pattern" DEF {
                ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 3
                ^"Rarity Modifier" STRING "+1"
                ^"Applies To" STRING "Weapon or armor"
                ^"Effect" STRING "The fearsome snarl pattern can be applied to a weapon or set of armor. It loses the Concealable quality (if it has it) and gains the Wargear quality."
            }

            #sUkovmEuTDAYIB0u2qlOpo ^"Ichiro Pattern" DEF {
                ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 4
                ^"Rarity Modifier" STRING "-1 (to a minimum of 1)"
                ^"Applies To" STRING "Weapon or armor"
                ^"Effect" STRING "Weapons or armor produced with the Ichirō pattern halve their price (rounding up) and lose the Ceremonial and Resplendent item qualities if they would otherwise have one or both qualities. Such items can never gain either quality. Ichirō pattern weapons and armor are also produced in half the time (rounding up) it would otherwise take to make them."
            }

            #0qJduuu2blFEcgzpx8WpTQ ^"Mountain Silk Pattern" DEF {
                ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 6
                ^"Rarity Modifier" STRING "+3"
                ^"Applies To" STRING "Armor"
                ^"Effect" STRING "When a character wearing armor made with mountain silk succeeds at a check to resist a critical strike, they add one bonus success. Armor with physical resistance 2 or lower made using mountain silk loses the Cumbersome quality (if it has it) and gains the Durable quality. Armor with physical resistance 3 or higher made using mountain silk gains the Durable quality and reduces its physical resistance by 1."
            }

            #m8Bvsg5pUgLg6qVNDjLmoY ^"Screaming Fire Pattern" DEF {
                ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 6
                ^"Rarity Modifier" STRING "+4"
                ^"Applies To" STRING "Blasting powder"
                ^"Effect" STRING "Blasting powder fashioned using the screaming fire pattern has its damage reduced by 2. When it causes an army to receive 1 or more panic during a Mass Battle, that army receives that amount of panic plus 3 instead. Additionally, the area it affects becomes Imbalanced (All Elements) for 1 week."
            }

            #eCiDUBwvlL5ET4tk3pOds3 ^"Toriyama's Endurance Pattern" DEF {
                ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 3
                ^"Rarity Modifier" STRING "+3"
                ^"Applies To" STRING "Parchment and scrolls"
                ^"Effect" STRING "Parchment and scrolls that are made with Toriyama's endurance pattern gain the Durable item quality, but only against the effects of fire and water."
            }
        }

        RULES {
            #L5RFV36vW7xY9zA1bC3dE5f: item_patterns "Item Patterns: Not all items are created equally. Depending on the smith or artisan and the materials used in its creation, weapons, armor, and even clothing can vary greatly, not just in style, but in performance. The patterns used in item creation are usually carefully guarded secrets, ones that a master would entrust only to the worthiest of their apprentices.\n\nThere are two methods for gaining an item with one of these patterns. The first is for a character to apprentice themselves to a master to learn the means of crafting a new item with the desired pattern; this requires the PC to win the master's trust within the story of the game and then to spend the XP to learn the pattern. The other method is to requisition, purchase, or find an existing item with the pattern. The price is the same, but the rarity is altered by the pattern's listed rarity modifier."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW TECHNIQUES
    # ===========================

    # source (page 95)
    #FCLdGhhdUL9fHv6Or5yPsb ^"Fields of Victory Techniques" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]

        ENTRIES {
            # --- CLOSE COMBAT KATA ---

            #WiiUOze5UTimhPZ3tvaOMt ^"Fierce Badger Style" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Kata"
                ^"Subtype" STRING "Close Combat Kata"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
                ^"Activation" STRING "When you make a Martial Arts [Unarmed] check targeting an a character at range 0, you may spend (op) in the following ways:"
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)+: If the target is Immobilized, they receive 1 strife per (op) spent this way. (op)+: If the target's silhouette and vigilance both are lower than or equal to (op) spent this way, the target is thrown 2 range bands in a direction of your choice and suffers 3 fatigue."
            }

            #F2WhSGS1JoRMy3ckJuGbb9 ^"Thicket's Embrace Style" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Kata"
                ^"Subtype" STRING "Close Combat Kata"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
                ^"Activation" STRING "When you make a Martial Arts [Unarmed] or Fitness check"
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op): If you are in Entangling or Obscuring terrain, reduce the TN of the next attack check you make by 1 (to a minimum of 1). This effect persists until the end of your next turn. (op)(op): If you are in Entangling or Obscuring terrain, you may ignore its negative effects. This effect persists until the end of your next turn."
            }

            #IrRoSBigG3z66ZLapW1LQd ^"Shattering Tide Style" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Kata"
                ^"Subtype" STRING "Close Combat Kata"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
                ^"Activation" STRING "When you make a Martial Arts [Unarmed] check"
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op): If you succeed, and both you and your target are in Confining or Dangerous terrain, treat the damage and deadliness of the weapon you used as 1 higher for each kept (st) result on your check. (op)(op): If both you and your target are in Confining or Dangerous terrain, your target suffers the Dazed condition."
            }

            # --- RITUALS ---

            #uhu7SYjHiK7fZphsuynezu ^"Beseech Akodo's Judgment" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Ritual"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
                ^"Activation" STRING "Once per game session as a Support action, you may make a TN 3 Tactics (Void) check targeting one terrain feature on the battlefield (or one battle zone, if using the rules for battle zones)"
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, increase your army's discipline by your glory rank plus your ranks in Command as long as your army has at least one cohort occupying the chosen terrain feature (or in that battle zone, if using the rules for battle zones). This effect persists until your army has no cohort occupying that feature (or zone), or until the end of the scene."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)+: If you succeed and designate a fortification (or a battle zone with a fortification in it), while your army occupies that fortification, increase that fortification's difficulty level by 1 per (op) spent this way.\n\n(op) (op)+: Each time your army suffers panic from battle fatigue during this scene, it suffers 1 less per (op) spent this way (to a minimum of 1)."
            }

            #rib8CRGkkCC5lLX3QoI7La ^"Beseech Bayushi's Absolution" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Ritual"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 4
                ^"Activation" STRING "Once per game session as a downtime activity, you may make a TN 3 Sentiment (Air) check targeting yourself"
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, the next time you would receive strife or fatigue, reduce the amount you receive by your focus. This effect persists until the end of the next scene."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op): If you succeed, the next time you would forfeit honor, reduce the amount you forfeit by half (rounded up)."
            }

            #Uyx3Q5xjrhlH6lVGLaGMuo ^"Beseech Doji's Wisdom" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Ritual"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
                ^"Activation" STRING "Once per game session as a downtime activity, you may make a TN 3 Composition check to transcribe a historical event you witnessed to paper. The event must have transpired within the recent past, before it has become well-known across the Empire."
                ^"Effect" STRING "You write from the heart to create a record of the event that rings a genuine account and omits no details of significance. Readers with vigilance lower than your honor rank trust the events to be true, or at least recorded in good faith."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "Fire (op): If you succeed, each character who is awarded one or more glory as a result of their involvement in this event receives that much glory plus your ranks in Culture instead.\n\nFire (op): If you succeed, choose one Great Clan or other major organization. The first time a character of that organization reads the text each scene, that character gains 2 strife.\n\nEarth (op): If you succeed, the text gains the Durable quality.\n\nEarth (op)+: If you succeed, when referencing the text as part of a check concerning the recorded historical event, reduce the TN of the check by your ranks in Government (to a minimum of 1).\n\nAir (op)+: If you succeed, you may omit one detail of significance per (op) spent this way without creating contradictions or obvious gaps in the text.\n\nAir (op) (op): If you succeed, choose one character. If that character is awarded one or more glory as a result of their involvement in this event, they receive double or half (your choice) that amount (rounded up) instead.\n\nWater (op): If you succeed, reduce the TN of any check to copy the text by 2 (to a minimum of 1).\n\nWater (op): If you succeed, choose one Great Clan or other major organization. The first time a character of that organization reads the text each scene, that character removes 2 strife.\n\nVoid (op) (op): The text becomes inhabited by a permanent blessing. It gains the Sacred item quality (see page 241 of the core rulebook)."
            }

            #9tRfTUVEqQttQnyyl3PNXp ^"Beseech Hida's Might" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Ritual"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
                ^"Activation" STRING "Once per game session as a downtime activity or Support action, you may make a TN 2 Meditation (Fire) check targeting an area encompassing 3 range bands around yourself"
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, this area becomes an arena. When a character makes a Martial Arts check in the arena during the event and does not gain strife from the check, that character reduces the TN of their next check by 1 (to a minimum of 1). This effect persists until the end of the next scene."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op): If you succeed, the arena gains the Hallowed (Fire) terrain quality until the end of the scene. (op)+: If you succeed, increase the Endurance and Composure of each character fighting a duel in the arena by 1 per (op) spent this way. (op)+: Reduce the TN of checks to remove the Bleeding and Dying conditions from characters within the arena by 1 per (op) spent this way (to a minimum of 1)."
            }

            #jvGI4C2UEc8x2OUbAJtQE9 ^"Beseech Shiba's Calm" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Ritual"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
                ^"Activation" STRING "Once per game session after participating in a Mass Battle or as a downtime activity, you may make a TN 3 Theology (Void) check targeting an area upon which a mass battle was fought earlier that day"
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, remove the Defiled terrain quality from the area."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op): If the area gained the Dangerous, Entangling, or Obscuring terrain quality during the battle through supernatural means, remove one or more of those terrain qualities of your choice.\n\n(op) (op): Remove the Imbalanced terrain quality from the area.\n\n(op) (op): Until the end of the game session, non-Tainted beings reduce the TN of Theology checks they make in this area by 1 (to a minimum of 1), and Tainted beings increase the TN of all checks they make in this area by 1.\n\n(op)+: Reduce the TN of any Fitness or Meditation checks that characters in your army need to make at the end of a scene by 1 per (op) spent this way, to a minimum of 1."
            }

            #la0OZXZOgaNKK56rl8pUwu ^"Beseech Shinjo's Empathy" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Ritual"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
                ^"Activation" STRING "Once per session as a downtime activity or Support action, you may make a Survival (Water) check targeting a friendly animal at range 0–1. The TN is equal to the (combat) conflict rank of the animal. If this is an animal you are bonded with (see page 111 of the core rulebook), reduce the TN of the check by 2 (to a minimum of 1)."
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, your target removes 3 fatigue, plus 1 additional fatigue per bonus success on the check."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op): You and the target each remove 1 strife per bonus success.\n\n(op): If you succeed, your target removes additional fatigue equal to your ranks in Medicine.\n\n(op): Remove the Bleeding condition from the target.\n\n(op) (op): Remove the Lightly Wounded condition from the target, or reduce the Severely Wounded condition to the Lightly Wounded condition.\n\n(op) (op): If you succeed, remove the Dying condition from the target.\n\n(op) (op)+: Choose one additional friendly animal of the same (combat) conflict rank or lower in range as a target per (op) spent this way."
            }

            #rWOZaWSDiAJKn56BGnTsdU ^"Beseech Togashi's Vision" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Ritual"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
                ^"Activation" STRING "Once per game session as a downtime activity or as a Scheme and Support action during a Mass Battle, you may make a TN 3 Meditation (Void) check targeting a character you can perceive (or a leader or commander of an enemy army in the scene)."
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, you assess another character's strategy. Once before the end of the next scene, after that character performs an action, you may reveal that you were prepared for this and immediately perform one action."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op): If you succeed and you are the commander of an army, you may choose a leader in your army to perform the action instead. (op): While you perform the prepared action, reduce the TN by your ranks in Tactics."
            }

            #VoFLDx1lH2ZjuTfndYjXaQ ^"Imbue Thunder" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Ritual"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 4
                ^"Activation" STRING "To perform this ritual, you must first assemble the proper ingredients (charred wood, salt of earth, pollen that burns) in the proper proportions. One full set of materials costs 10 koku and has a rarity of 6, and is consumed by the process. Once per session as a downtime activity, you may make a TN 4 Medicine check to properly mix the ingredients to create blasting powder."
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, you create ten brilliant flares (see 90), plus ten per two bonus successes, or one blasting powder charge (see page 90), plus one per two bonus successes."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op) (op): When used in a skirmish, the charge inflicts the Dazed condition on all characters at range 0–4.\n\nAir (op) (op): When used in a skirmish, increase the charge's range band by 1.\n\nEarth (op) (op)+: When used, the charge inflicts 2 additional damage (or attrition) per (op) (op) spent this way.\n\nFire (op) (op)+: When used, the charge inflicts 2 additional strife (or panic) per (op) (op) spent this way.\n\nWater (op) (op): When used in a skirmish, the charge inflicts the Bleeding condition on all characters at range 0–2.\n\nVoid (op) (op): When used, the charge frightens away all kami in the radius of effect (or across the entire battlefield, in a mass battle). The affected area becomes Imbalanced (All Elements) terrain. This effect persists for 1 day."
            }

            # --- AIR SHUJI ---

            #h37W6ZKcuH1aay8pxtKqa2 ^"Borrowed Courage" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
                ^"Subtype" STRING "Air Shūji"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 1
                ^"Activation" STRING "As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 4 Performance (Air) check targeting an army or a number of characters who can hear you up to your ranks in Sentiment. You may stake up to 3 honor to reduce the TN by that amount (to a minimum of 1) to embellish the truth."
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, you spread a powerful rumor of your foe's weakness, of allies certain to arrive, or of some other hidden advantage that should ensure victory. The first time your target receives panic or strife during the next scene, they reduce the amount they receive by your ranks in Performance, to a minimum of 0.\n\nWhether you succeed or fail, if your side loses the battle, you lose your staked honor (as your boasts proved false). Additionally, there might be narrative social ramifications should individuals remember the lies you told."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "Air (op): If you fail, nobody remembers exactly what you said, so there are no narrative social consequences for your fabrication.\n\nAir (op): Add 1 kept (ring) set to (op) to the first Scheme action check you make during the next mass battle your army fights."
            }

            #i3Ktgc1rQ9WEofHJrQoTy7 ^"Clouds Parted by Steel" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
                ^"Subtype" STRING "Air Shūji"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
                ^"Activation" STRING "When you make a check to perform a Strike action (see page 264 of the core rulebook) or an Assault action (see page 278 of the core rulebook), you may spend (op) as follows:"
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "Air (op)+: If your target's vigilance is lower than your ranks in Sentiment plus (op) spent this way, choose one of the advantage/disadvantage types: interpersonal, mental, or physical. If your target has one or more advantages or disadvantages of that type, you learn what they are."
            }

            #KbVL2P4Zz9yQFLP3QBubmb ^"Entice with Falsehoods" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
                ^"Subtype" STRING "Air Shūji"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 4
                ^"Activation" STRING "Once per scene during a mass battle as a Scheme action targeting the commander of the enemy army, you may make a Tactics (Air) check. The TN is equal to the target's vigilance. If you are not your army's commander, you must stake 5 honor and 5 glory on your success. If your cohort is in Obscuring terrain, reduce the TN by 2."
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, you immediately change your army's current strategic goal to a new goal of your choice. Any momentum points your army had accrued toward the previous goal are applied to this new goal.\n\nIf you fail and you are not the commander, your commander's scorn falls upon you for overstepping your position. You lose your staked honor and glory."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "Air (op): Your target remains unaware of your machinations.\n\nAir (op): Gain 1 momentum point toward your army's current strategic objective.\n\nAir (op)+: All characters in the scene with vigilance lower than or equal to (op) spent this way are unaware of your machinations."
            }

            # --- EARTH SHUJI ---

            #Y4ExqealyrjNSVmSFr8BKz ^"Fortress of Necessity" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
                ^"Subtype" STRING "Earth Shūji"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 1
                ^"Activation" STRING "As a downtime activity or a Support action during a mass battle, using adequate supplies and a suitable area, you may make a TN 3 Command (Earth) check targeting a position you can reach"
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, you erect a defensive structure of trenches or short barricades in the area. In a mass battle, this structure is treated as a fortification with difficulty value equal to your ranks in Labor plus your bonus successes, which reduces attrition suffered by the cohort occupying it by 2. In a skirmish, this structure is treated as Obscuring terrain by anyone attacking those inside from outside. This structure is temporary, and degrades completely if left to the elements for more than a few days. It can be maintained with a TN 2 Labor (Earth) check as a downtime activity, which might need to be made more frequently in harsh weather conditions such as rain or snow."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "Earth (op): When you perform the Reinforce action in this fortification during a mass battle, treat the TN as reduced by 1 (to a minimum of 1).\n\nEarth (op) (op)+: Add one of the following terrain qualities per (op) (op) spent this way to the area extending from range 1–3 around the building: Dangerous, Entangling, Obscuring, or Recessed. During a mass battle, enemies attacking a cohort in the fortification are treated as being in terrain with the added qualities."
            }

            #c4KvPwB5uGyV658OSHDJK9 ^"Great Anvil's Measure" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
                ^"Subtype" STRING "Earth Shūji"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
                ^"Activation" STRING "When you make a check to perform a Guard action in a skirmish (see page 264 of the core rulebook) or a Reinforce action in a mass battle (see page 279 of the core rulebook), you may spend (op) as follows:"
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "Earth (op)+ (Guard): Choose any number of characters in the scene with focus lower than or equal to your ranks in Performance plus 2 per (op) spent this way. Each chosen character must receive strife equal to your ranks in Performance to perform an Attack or Scheme action targeting any character other than you. This effect persists until the end of your next turn.\n\nEarth (op)+ (Reinforce): Choose any number of leaders in the enemy army with focus lower than or equal to your ranks in Performance plus 2 per (op) spent this way. The enemy army receives panic equal to your ranks in Performance each time any of those leaders performs an Attack or Scheme action targeting any cohort other than yours. This effect persists until the end of your next turn."
            }

            #S8oDesz1LIaDdYS0V18bS1 ^"Steady the Hammer" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
                ^"Subtype" STRING "Earth Shūji"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 4
                ^"Activation" STRING "As an Attack and Support action during a mass battle, you may make a TN 5 Tactics (Earth) check targeting one enemy leader's cohort that performed an Attack action check targeting your cohort this round. If that enemy cohort is in Confining, Entangling, or Recessed terrain, reduce the TN to 2."
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, decrease the TN of the next Attack action check made by a friendly leader that targets that cohort by 1 plus your bonus successes (to a minimum of 1). If that check succeeds, add additional bonus successes equal to your ranks in Command. This effect persists until the end of the round."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "Earth (op)+: This effect applies to one additional Attack action check made by a friendly cohort before the end of the round per (op) spent this way."
            }

            # --- FIRE SHUJI ---

            #JsORqVBbGU90uyrtQRQ7xt ^"Call the Wild" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
                ^"Subtype" STRING "Fire Shūji"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
                ^"Activation" STRING "As a Support action, you may make a Survival (Fire) check targeting one friendly animal or manifest kami at range 0–2. The TN of the check is equal to the animal or kami's (combat) conflict rank."
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, increase the damage and deadliness of the animal or kami's weapon profiles by 1, plus 1 for every two bonus successes beyond the first. This effect persists until the end of the scene."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)+: You may target one additional friendly animal or manifest kami per (op) spent this way.\n\n(op)+: The target animal or kami removes 1 fatigue per (op) spent this way.\n\n(op): The animal gains the Enraged condition, then removes all strife."
            }

            #UQ7tsy5zsi4HEBifu1tLoK ^"Righteous Example" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
                ^"Subtype" STRING "Fire Shūji"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 1
                ^"Activation" STRING "As an Attack and Support action during a mass battle, you may make a TN 3 Martial Arts (Fire) check targeting an enemy leader's cohort"
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, the enemy army suffers attrition and panic equal to 1 plus your bonus successes.\n\nIf you succeed, other leaders in your army reduce the TN of their Attack action checks by 1. This effect persists until the end of your next turn.\n\nIf you fail, reduce the TN of Attack and Scheme action checks targeting your cohort by 1. This effect persists until the end of your next turn."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "Fire (op)(op): If you are both the commander and a leader, your army gains 1 momentum point toward its current strategic objective."
            }

            #gLkPuxnpoRqK9TYQRizqGl ^"Sting of Warrior's Pride" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
                ^"Subtype" STRING "Fire Shūji"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
                ^"Activation" STRING "As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 4 Performance (Fire) check targeting an army or one character who can hear you. You may stake up to 3 glory to reduce the TN by that amount (to a minimum of 1)."
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, you spur your target to greater courage in the face of death. The first time your target is dealt attrition or damage during the next scene, they reduce the amount by your ranks in Performance, to a minimum of 0.\n\nWhether you succeed or fail, if you are observed acting in a cowardly manner by your target during the scene, you lose any glory you staked on this technique."
            }

            #GJWnN4dauM15tiZYDWXxb8 ^"To Smash the Heart" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
                ^"Subtype" STRING "Fire Shūji"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 4
                ^"Activation" STRING "Once per scene, after a character in the scene (or enemy leader, in a mass battle) becomes Compromised or is killed, you may immediately make a TN 4 Tactics (Fire) check targeting that character"
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed in an intrigue, skirmish, or duel, each character in the scene allied with your target who has lower status than your target receives strife equal to your bonus successes plus your ranks in Sentiment.\n\nIf you succeed in a mass battle, the enemy army receives panic equal to your bonus successes plus your ranks in Sentiment."
            }

            # --- WATER SHUJI ---

            #nx1afKxRgLIWsZznmM2jAh ^"Coursing March Chant" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
                ^"Subtype" STRING "Water Shūji"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 1
                ^"Activation" STRING "As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 4 Performance (Water) check targeting an army or targeting a number of characters traveling with you up to your ranks in Command. You may expend an additional day's rations (army rations for an army, individual rations for an individual) to reduce the TN by 2 (to a minimum of 1)."
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, you and your targets can march twice the distance they normally could in that time."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "Water (op): If your target is an army, it removes attrition up to your ranks in Medicine.\n\nWater (op): If your target is an army, it removes panic up to your ranks in Culture.\n\nWater (op)+: One individual target per (op) spent this way removes fatigue up to your ranks in Medicine.\n\nWater (op)+: One individual target per (op) spent this way removes strife up to your ranks in Culture.\n\nWater (op) (op)+: Choose one mundane terrain quality that would normally affect the targets on the march per (op) (op) spent this way. Each target ignores that terrain quality during the march."
            }

            #V4Ev8uTaQZplr7RFQFagq1 ^"Preserve Strength" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
                ^"Subtype" STRING "Water Shūji"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
                ^"Activation" STRING "Once per scene as a Support action or as a downtime activity, you may direct triage by making a TN 3 Medicine (Water) check targeting a friendly army or a number of characters at range 0–3 up to your ranks in Command."
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed during a mass battle, your target removes 5 casualties, plus 1 for every two bonus successes.\n\nIf you succeed during a skirmish, each of your targets reduces the TN of their next Medicine check by 2, plus 1 for every two bonus successes (to a minimum of 1)."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "Water (op) (op) (Mass Battle): If you succeed, choose a friendly leader in the target army. Remove one of the following conditions from that character: Bleeding, Burning, Dying.\n\nWater (op) (op) (Skirmish): If you succeed, each of your targets may immediately move 1 range band, or 2 range bands toward a character who is suffering the Bleeding, Burning, or Dying condition."
            }

            #XMipKgmtcelXCBUko84K8U ^"Your Enemy's Arrows" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
                ^"Subtype" STRING "Water Shūji"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 4
                ^"Activation" STRING "Once per scene as a Scheme action targeting another character who can perceive you or your cohort, you may make a Tactics (Water) check. The TN is equal to the target's focus. You may stake up to 3 glory on your success to reduce the TN by that amount."
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, the next time your target accrues momentum points toward an objective, add those momentum points to your objective instead.\n\nIf you fail, you lose the glory you staked upon your success."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "Water (op): Your target remains unaware of your machinations. If you failed, regain your staked glory.\n\nWater (op): Gain 1 momentum point toward your current goal.\n\nWater (op)+: All characters in the scene with vigilance lower than or equal to (op) spent this way are unaware of your machinations."
            }

            # --- VOID SHUJI ---

            #sOAprLVAYXiYFAMDSflMNu ^"Battle of No Escape" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
                ^"Subtype" STRING "Void Shūji"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
                ^"Activation" STRING "Once per scene as a Support action, you may make a TN 5 Command (Void) check targeting your cohort or a number of characters who can hear you up to your ranks in Meditation. Reduce the TN of this check to 2 if all targets are in Confining or Entangling terrain."
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed during a mass battle, your army does not suffer morale collapse if its panic exceeds its discipline, and continues to function normally. This effect persists for one round, plus one round for every three bonus successes.\n\nIf you succeed during an intrigue, duel, or skirmish, each target ignores the effects of the Compromised condition. This effect persists for one round, plus one round for every two bonus successes."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "Void (op)+ (Intrigue, Duel, or Skirmish): Choose one additional target per (op) spent this way.\n\nVoid (op) (op) (Intrigue, Duel, or Skirmish): If you succeed, each target also ignores the effects of the Incapacitated condition for one round, plus one round for every two bonus successes."
            }

            #MYc4PvL5ENlyPKVprqTaGT ^"Moment of Glory" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
                ^"Subtype" STRING "Void Shūji"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
                ^"Activation" STRING "Once per scene as an a Movement and Support action during a mass battle, you may make a TN 4 Meditation (Void) check. Reduce the TN of this check to 2 if your cohort is in Confining or Obscuring terrain."
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, whenever your cohort is targeted with an Attack action check, reduce any attrition it inflicts on your army to 0, and receive that much fatigue yourself instead. If fatigue you receive this way causes you to suffer a critical strike, the severity is 16. This effect persists until the start of your next turn."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "Void (op)+: If you succeed, while this effect persists, reduce any fatigue you receive by 1 per (op) spent this way (to a minimum of 0).\n\nVoid (op) (op): If you succeed, if you suffer a critical strike this way, it is not applied until the end of the scene, at which point you receive any critical strike results you deferred this way.\n\nVoid (op): If you succeed and you survive, double any glory you are awarded from your action."
            }

            #Vf4DLGLNbHVJb7CiQGkHG4 ^"Victory Without a Sword" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
                ^"Subtype" STRING "Void Shūji"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 6
                ^"Activation" STRING "As an Attack, Movement, Scheme, and Support action during a mass battle, you may make a TN 6 Tactics (Void) check targeting the enemy commander. Reduce the TN of this check to 4 if all cohorts of the enemy army are in Dangerous, Entangling, or Obscuring terrain. This technique can only be attempted once per army per scene."
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, the enemy commander immediately resists with a TN 5 Command check (Void 3), adding 1 to the TN for every 10 strength your army has in excess of the enemy army's strength. If the enemy commander succeeds, their army suffers no ill effects. If the enemy commander fails, the enemy army suffers 10 panic for each point of their shortfall. If the enemy army collapses this way, its forces surrender. Individual leaders may choose whether they wish to withdraw or hold the line as their troops surrender.\n\nIf you fail, reduce the TN of Attack action checks targeting the cohorts of leaders in your army by 2 (to a minimum of 1). This effect persists until the end of the scene."
            }

            # --- NINJUTSU ---

            #8FTMF995xakcuJRgZB5IDZ ^"Employ Terrible Thunder" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Ninjutsu"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
                ^"Activation" STRING "As a Movement and Support action, you may make a TN 4 Skulduggery check and expend 1 charge of blasting powder (see page 90) to place it in your environment at a target position at range 0–1 of you. You must forfeit honor equal to equal to half your honor rank (rounded up) to use this technique."
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, you set the blasting powder to explode at the end of the next round. Some or all of the following occur based on the scene type:\n\n(Mass Battle) Any nearby cohort (such as those in the same zone, if using the rules for zones on page 118) is caught by the blast, and that army receives 5 attrition and 5 panic, plus 1 per bonus success.\n\n(Mass Battle) If you placed the blasting powder inside of a fortification (see the Fortifications sidebar on page 276 of the core rulebook), reduce its difficulty value by 1, plus 1 per bonus success.\n\n(Mass Battle) One cohort leader affected by the explosion suffers the Immobilized and Lightly Wounded conditions.\n\n(Other Scene) Each character at range 0–2 of the target position suffers 10 physical damage plus 1 per bonus success, suffers the Dazed condition, and receives 5 strife.\n\n(Other Scene) Items at range 0–2 of the target position gain the Damaged item quality.\n\n(Other Scene) Any structure (such as a bridge, house, or wall) at range 0–1 of the target position gains the Damaged quality."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op): Any item or structure damaged by this effect gains the Destroyed quality instead.\n\n(op) (op): The area at range 0–2 of the position of the explosion gains the Dangerous and Obscuring terrain qualities, and flammable objects in the area are set ablaze.\n\n(op)+: The blasting powder does not detonate for one additional round per (op) spent this way."
            }

            #HSzt420vwOR9WKhZyQc8A4 ^"Swift Scouting" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Ninjutsu"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 1
                ^"Activation" STRING "As a downtime activity, or once per scene as a Movement and Support action, you may make a TN 3 Survival (Water) check to scout the terrain around you. If you activate this technique in an urban environment or on the ocean, use Skulduggery or Seafaring instead, respectively."
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, you discover all terrain qualities of the area around you (several miles in all direction during downtime, or the entire area in which the scene is occurring), as well as any fortifications in the area. Characters with vigilance lower than your Air Ring plus your bonus successes do not detect you during this time."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "Water (op) (op) (Downtime or Mass Battle): If you succeed, you may choose one part of the area (a single battle zone, if using the rules for battle zones) and add one of the following terrain qualities to that area: Confining, Dangerous, Entangling, Obscuring.\n\nWater (op) (op) (Other Scene): If you succeed, you may choose a position in the area you scouted. Up to three range bands surrounding that position gain one of the following terrain qualities: Confining, Dangerous, Entangling, Obscuring.\n\nWater (op)+: You discover the location and composition of any enemy forces in the area led by characters with Air Ring lower than your vigilance plus (op) spent this way.\n\nWater (op) (op) (op): During your next turn, if you perform an action targeting an enemy cohort, ignore any fortification it is occupying. You may resolve effects as if you were inside that fortification."
            }

            #fbWIpV8KvO0fta0DnPmJKE ^"The Patient Viper" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Ninjutsu"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
                ^"Activation" STRING "As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 4 Fitness (Earth) check targeting your cohort (if you are currently the leader of a cohort) or yourself and a number of other characters up to your ranks in Command (in any other scene) who are within Dangerous, Entangling, or Obscuring terrain."
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, all targets become hidden and are not noticed by characters with vigilance lower than or equal to your Earth Ring plus your bonus successes. These hidden characters cannot be the target of Attack actions. This effect persists until the end of your next turn, or until any target you have hidden performs an Attack or Movement action."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "Earth (op)+: This effect persists for one additional round per (op) spent this way.\n\nEarth (op)+: Reduce the TN of the first Attack action check one of your targets makes against another character in the terrain in which your forces are hidden by 1 per (op) spent this way."
            }

            #KgZOYwtz9t7tKljuhS4Amz ^"Vanish in the Shadows" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Ninjutsu"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
                ^"Activation" STRING "As a downtime activity or once per scene as a Movement and Support action, you may make a TN 5 Survival (Air) check targeting your cohort (in a mass battle) or yourself and a number of characters up to your ranks in Command (in any other scene) who are within Confining, Entangling, or Obscuring terrain. If you activate this technique in an urban environment or on the ocean, use Skulduggery or Seafaring instead, respectively."
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, all targets become hidden and are not noticed by characters with vigilance lower than or equal to your Air Ring plus your bonus successes. These hidden characters cannot be the target of Attack actions and cannot perform Attack actions. This effect persists until the end of your next turn, or until any target performs an Attack action."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "Air (op)+ (Mass Battle): If you succeed, if an enemy army has one or more cohorts within the terrain, it receives 1 panic per (op) spent this way.\n\nAir (op)+ (Other Scene): If you succeed, each character you did not target who is within the terrain receives 1 strife per (op) spent this way.\n\nAir (op) (op) (op): If you failed, increase the TN of Attack action checks targeting each of your targets by 2. This effect persists until any of your targets performs an Attack action or leaves the terrain."
            }

            #peXoVvwtjO90UQRw0eHl4B ^"Wreak Havoc" DEF {
                ^"Type" STRING "Ninjutsu"
                ^"Rank" INTEGER 4
                ^"Activation" STRING "Once per game session as an Attack and Movement action during a mass battle, you may make a Skulduggery (Fire) check targeting one enemy leader's cohort. The TN is equal to the vigilance of that cohort's leader. You may expend 1 charge of blasting powder and forfeit honor equal to half your honor rank (rounded up) to reduce the TN by 2 (to a minimum of 1)."
                ^"Effect" STRING "If you succeed, you achieve one of the following:\n\nReduce the difficulty value of a fortification the target is occupying by 4 plus your bonus successes. If this reduces the difficulty value to 0 or lower, the fortification is destroyed; any army with a cohort occupying it receives attrition equal to your bonus successes, and any leader or commander inside suffers a critical strike severity equal to 6 plus your bonus successes.\n\nRemove the Confining and Entangling terrain quality from a fortification the target cohort occupies, but add the Dangerous and Obscuring terrain qualities to that area as it catches ablaze.\n\nRemove one cohort ability from the target cohort. This ability is restored when the army resupplies (such as when making a maintenance check, as described on page 115).\n\nAdditionally, if you succeed, the target leader must resist with a TN 5 Command check (Air 6, Water 3) or their army suffers panic equal to your ranks in Performance plus their shortfall."
                ^"Opportunities" STRING "Fire (op): If you succeed, the target cohort's leader suffers a critical strike with severity equal to equal to 6 plus your bonus successes.\n\nFire (op) (op): The target cohort's leader suffers the Dazed condition.\n\nFire (op)+: If you succeed, you may expend a number of additional charges of blasting powder up to (op) spent this way to add two bonus successes per charge expended this way."
            }
        }

        RULES {
            #L5RFV37gH8iJ0kL2mN4oP6q: new_techniques "New Techniques: The following are new techniques that samurai from the Lion and other clans can use to lead armies and engage in battle on behalf of their clan and the Empire."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # TITLES
    # ===========================

    # source (pages 131-137)
    #Fpv77T5pFQz6RaZ2EN4KNb ^"Fields of Victory Titles" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]

        ENTRIES {
            #bO7tCRp7pdtrONrgRvrCNe ^"Ashigaru" DEF {
                ^"Assigned By" STRING "Any samurai officer. You must survive at least one mass battle to receive this title."
                ^"Glory Award" STRING "+5 (to a maximum of 29)"
                ^"Status Award" STRING "+3 (to a maximum of 19)"
                ^"XP to Completion" INTEGER 20
                ^"Title Ability" STRING "A Thousand Stinging Cuts"
                ^"Title Ability Effect" STRING "When you provide assistance (see page 26 of the core rulebook) on the Martial Arts [Melee] Attack action check of another character at range 0–2, the character you are assisting treats their target's physical resistance as 1 lower for each assisting character with this ability."
                ^"Advancement" LIST OF STRING [
                    "Martial Skills (Skill Group)",
                    "Courtesy (Skill)",
                    "Command (Skill)",
                    "Survival (Skill)",
                    "Rank 1-2 Kata (kata) (Tech Group)",
                    "Thicket's Embrace Style (kata)",
                    "Slippery Maneuvers (shuji)"
                ]
            }

            #PNdXQD5zE3K5QTVcEbHBCl ^"Deathseeker" DEF {
                ^"Assigned By" STRING "Disgraced Lion Clan samurai may take this title upon themselves, pending approval from the GM."
                ^"Status Award" STRING "-25 (to a minimum of 20)"
                ^"XP to Completion" INTEGER 8
                ^"Immediate Effects" STRING "You give up any positions you hold and your worldly possessions, save one weapon and a set of ceremonial robes, are returned to your family."
                ^"Title Ability" STRING "Kirifu's Oath"
                ^"Title Ability Effect" STRING "As a Support action, you may suffer the Enraged condition (see page 272 of the core rulebook).\n\nWhile you are Enraged, you can perform Attack actions even while Incapacitated."
                ^"Advancement" LIST OF STRING [
                    "Martial Skills (Skill Group)",
                    "Command (Skill)",
                    "Government (Skill)",
                    "Medicine (Skill)",
                    "Beseech Shiba's Calm (ritual)",
                    "Tactical Assessment (kata)",
                    "Warrior's Resolve (kata)"
                ]
            }

            #xBZNL0T3mCVhL3Sp3jPOKY ^"Elemental Guard" DEF {
                ^"Assigned By" STRING "An Elemental Master."
                ^"Glory Award" STRING "+10"
                ^"Status Award" STRING "+10"
                ^"XP to Completion" INTEGER 20
                ^"Title Ability" STRING "Wrath of the Elements"
                ^"Title Ability Effect" STRING "Choose one: Air, Earth, Fire, or Water. This is your elemental specialty. Once per scene after making a Martial skill check that uses the ring of your elemental specialty, you may inflict an amount of strife or panic equal to your ranks in the ring associated with your elemental specialty against a target at range 0–3 or a cohort in the scene."
                ^"Advancement" LIST OF STRING [
                    "Martial Skills (Skill Group)",
                    "Courtesy (Skill)",
                    "Labor (Skill)",
                    "Theology (Skill)",
                    "Rank 1-3 Kata (kata) (Tech Group)",
                    "A Samurai's Fate (shuji)",
                    "Moment of Glory (shuji)"
                ]
            }

            #8IECWrsBZ8OrNycFawg4JX ^"Elemental Legionnaire" DEF {
                ^"Assigned By" STRING "A daimyō of the Shiba family or the Phoenix Clan Champion, with permission from a member of the Elemental Council."
                ^"Glory Award" STRING "+10"
                ^"Status Award" STRING "+10"
                ^"XP to Completion" INTEGER 24
                ^"Title Ability" STRING "Strength of the Elements"
                ^"Title Ability Effect" STRING "Choose one: Air, Earth, Fire, or Water. This is your elemental specialty. Once per scene after making a Martial skill check that uses the ring of your elemental specialty, you and a number of targets at range 0–3 (or other cohort leaders in the scene) up to your ranks in Command may remove strife equal to your ranks in the ring associated with your elemental specialty."
                ^"Advancement" LIST OF STRING [
                    "Martial Skills (Skill Group)",
                    "Command (Skill)",
                    "Medicine (Skill)",
                    "Smithing (Skill)",
                    "Rank 1-3 Kata (kata) (Tech Group)",
                    "Great Anvil's Measure (shuji)",
                    "Moment of Glory (shuji)"
                ]
            }

            #brn5dYSnqrAFrJMQ4KApRh ^"General" DEF {
                ^"Assigned By" STRING "A clan or family daimyō with a status of 60 or higher, often following a great military achievement by the character."
                ^"Glory Award" STRING "+10"
                ^"Status Award" STRING "+25 (to a maximum of 85)"
                ^"XP to Completion" INTEGER 50
                ^"Title Ability" STRING "Superior Command"
                ^"Title Ability Effect" STRING "While you are the commander of an army during a mass battle, your army's discipline value is increased by your ranks in Command. Additionally, when making an Initiative check during a mass battle, increase the result by your ranks in Tactics."
                ^"Advancement" LIST OF STRING [
                    "Social Skills (Skill Group)",
                    "Martial Skills (Skill Group)",
                    "Government (Skill)",
                    "Survival (Skill)",
                    "Rank 1-2 Kata (kata) (Tech Group)",
                    "Rank 1-3 Rituals (ritual) (Tech Group)",
                    "Rank 1-4 Shūji (shuji) (Tech Group)"
                ]
            }

            #91XMcaJ3so9PBn3aDp493X ^"Lion's Pride Warrior" DEF {
                ^"Assigned By" STRING "An existing member of the Lion's Pride."
                ^"Glory Award" STRING "+10"
                ^"Status Award" STRING "+20 (to a maximum of 59)"
                ^"XP to Completion" INTEGER 24
                ^"Title Ability" STRING "Fury of Matsu"
                ^"Title Ability Effect" STRING "Once per scene, when you deal damage to a target or deal attrition to an enemy leader's cohort, increase the damage or attrition by an amount equal to the difference between your honor rank and the target's honor rank."
                ^"Advancement" LIST OF STRING [
                    "Martial Skills (Skill Group)",
                    "Command (Skill)",
                    "Sentiment (Skill)",
                    "Survival (Skill)",
                    "Rank 1-3 Kata (kata) (Tech Group)",
                    "A Samurai's Fate (shuji)",
                    "Battle of No Escape (shuji)"
                ]
            }

            #a8OptrJhTxJkmeZgcQiOe5 ^"Master Saboteur" DEF {
                ^"Assigned By" STRING "Three other master saboteurs, who are usually members of a general's command staff or found leading specialized clandestine units."
                ^"Status Award" STRING "None"
                ^"XP to Completion" INTEGER 40
                ^"Title Ability" STRING "Ender of Works"
                ^"Title Ability Effect" STRING "When a fortification's difficulty value would be reduced during a mass battle, the value is lowered by that amount plus your ranks in Labor instead. If there is a cohort occupying it, that cohort's army suffers panic equal to your ranks in Skulduggery."
                ^"Advancement" LIST OF STRING [
                    "Trade Skills (Skill Group)",
                    "Government (Skill)",
                    "Martial Arts [Unarmed] (Skill)",
                    "Medicine (Skill)",
                    "Rank 1-2 Ninjutsu (ninjutsu) (Tech Group)",
                    "Imbue Thunder (ritual)",
                    "Wreak Havoc (ninjutsu)"
                ]
            }

            #FKmNyCeiPathHFblUNfqTa ^"Poet of War" DEF {
                ^"Assigned By" STRING "A general or other officer with status 50 or higher."
                ^"Glory Award" STRING "+10 (to a maximum of 55)"
                ^"XP to Completion" INTEGER 20
                ^"Title Ability" STRING "The Hand of Our Ancestors"
                ^"Title Ability Effect" STRING "After you perform a successful Rally action, the targeted cohort deals 1 additional attrition when its leader performs a successful Attack action check. This effect persists for one round."
                ^"Advancement" LIST OF STRING [
                    "Social Skills (Skill Group)",
                    "Composition (Skill)",
                    "Culture (Skill)",
                    "Sentiment (Skill)",
                    "Rank 1-2 Fire Shūji (shuji) (Tech Group)",
                    "Borrowed Courage (shuji)",
                    "Coursing March Chant (shuji)"
                ]
            }

            #C0cszxeIzLT4uFG9zvF4ey ^"Quartermaster" DEF {
                ^"Assigned By" STRING "Clan or castle daimyō, army general, or other officer of sufficient rank."
                ^"Status Award" STRING "+5 (to a maximum of 35)"
                ^"XP to Completion" INTEGER 24
                ^"Title Ability" STRING "Procurement and Supply"
                ^"Title Ability Effect" STRING "When you make a check as a downtime activity to provision an army, you may spend (op) as follows:\n\n(op)+: If you succeed, your army increases its discipline and strength each by 1 per (op) spent this way. This effect persists until the end of the next mass battle scene."
                ^"Advancement" LIST OF STRING [
                    "Trade Skills (Skill Group)",
                    "Courtesy (Skill)",
                    "Government (Skill)",
                    "Tactics (Skill)",
                    "Rank 1-2 Air Shūji (shuji) (Tech Group)",
                    "Rank 1-2 Water Shūji (shuji) (Tech Group)",
                    "Fortress of Necessity (shuji)"
                ]
            }

            #xfmn5zLJZB4SrYpBZBh27R ^"Renowned Warrior" DEF {
                ^"Assigned By" STRING "A daimyō or army commander with status 60 or higher after you have been part of a mass battle in which your cohort was the one to complete at least one strategic objective."
                ^"Glory Award" STRING "+5"
                ^"Status Award" STRING "+5 (to a maximum of 40)"
                ^"XP to Completion" INTEGER 16
                ^"Title Ability" STRING "Behold the Legend"
                ^"Title Ability Effect" STRING "Once per scene, after you make a successful Martial Arts check that inflicts fatigue or a critical strike on the target, you may have each friendly character at range 0-3 of you or the target remove an amount of strife equal to the TN of the check."
                ^"Advancement" LIST OF STRING [
                    "Martial Skills (Skill Group)",
                    "Command (Skill)",
                    "Culture (Skill)",
                    "Performance (Skill)",
                    "Rank 1-2 Kata (kata) (Tech Group)",
                    "Heartpiercing Strike (kata)",
                    "Righteous Example (shuji)"
                ]
            }

            #wILK5uQ1fgm5LH2qilvaxS ^"Spirit Caller" DEF {
                ^"Assigned By" STRING "An instructor of a Kitsu school or other appropriate spiritual leader."
                ^"Status Award" STRING "+15 (to a maximum of 40)"
                ^"XP to Completion" INTEGER 38
                ^"Title Ability" STRING "Eyes of the Ancestors"
                ^"Title Ability Effect" STRING "Once per game session as a Support action, you may spend 1 Void point to summon the spirit of an ancestor to partially possess you until the end of the scene. Choose a ring and a skill from that ancestor's profile; while possessed, you count as an Otherworldly being and use your ancestor's ring value and skill rank in place of your own, as well as your ancestor's honor value. Your ancestor can use any non-unique human NPC profile (or a kitsu's or other supernatural being's profile, if your character has such an ancestor). The higher of this NPC's (combat) conflict rank and (intrigue) conflict rank cannot exceed your school rank plus your ranks in Meditation. While you are possessed, the ancestor spirit may divulge pertinent information at the GM's discretion. Afterward, your character will have only a hazy memory of anything they experienced while possessed."
                ^"Advancement" LIST OF STRING [
                    "Scholar Skills (Skill Group)",
                    "Courtesy (Skill)",
                    "Meditation (Skill)",
                    "Performance (Skill)",
                    "Rank 1-2 Rituals (ritual) (Tech Group)",
                    "Ancestry Unearthed (shuji)",
                    "Preserve Strength (shuji)"
                ]
            }

            #IkqasINI1gevVsPe3Yg4Qa ^"Sumai Master" DEF {
                ^"Assigned By" STRING "An existing sumai master, once you have proven your ability to them."
                ^"Glory Award" STRING "+10 (to a maximum of 50)"
                ^"Status Award" STRING "+10 (to a minimum of 35)"
                ^"XP to Completion" INTEGER 30
                ^"Title Ability" STRING "Unsurpassed Soul"
                ^"Title Ability Effect" STRING "When you make a Martial Arts [Unarmed] check targeting another character, if your Void ring is higher than or equal to your target's Void ring, reduce the TN by 2 (to a minimum of 1)."
                ^"Advancement" LIST OF STRING [
                    "Social Skills (Skill Group)",
                    "Culture (Skill)",
                    "Martial Arts [Unarmed] (Skill)",
                    "Theology (Skill)",
                    "Rank 1-2 Kata (kata) (Tech Group)",
                    "Beseech Hida's Might (ritual)",
                    "Fierce Badger Style (kata)"
                ]
            }

            #6SoUaVJEHdot0Vn4b1NSoG ^"Sword-Saint" DEF {
                ^"Assigned By" STRING "A clan champion or the Emperor. Alternately, the title can be assigned by an existing sword-saint who is slain by the character in an honorable duel to the death."
                ^"Glory Award" STRING "+20 (to a maximum of 100)"
                ^"XP to Completion" INTEGER 24
                ^"Title Ability" STRING "Invincible Blade"
                ^"Title Ability Effect" STRING "When you perform an Attack or Support action check that uses a sword, you may spend (op) as follows:\n\nVoid (op)+: Reduce the severity of the next critical strike you would suffer (before your Fitness check to resist) by your ranks in Meditation plus 1 per (op) spent this way. This effect persists until the start of your next turn.\n\nAny (op) (op): Increase the base damage and deadliness of your weapon by 3. This effect persists until the end of the scene. If you activate this (op) multiple times during a scene, the effect is cumulative (add together all increases you have applied this scene with this (op))."
                ^"Advancement" LIST OF STRING [
                    "Martial Arts [Melee] (Skill)",
                    "Meditation (Skill)",
                    "Smithing (Skill)",
                    "Tactics (Skill)",
                    "Rank 1-5 Close Combat Kata (kata) (Tech Group)",
                    "Soul Sunder (kata)",
                    "Victory Without a Sword (shuji)"
                ]
            }

            #k4XtSdnKFxMEYqM2cG6kbz ^"War College Graduate" DEF {
                ^"Assigned By" STRING "An instructor at the Akodo War College."
                ^"Glory Award" STRING "+5 (to a maximum of 60)"
                ^"Status Award" STRING "+10 (to a maximum of 40)"
                ^"XP to Completion" INTEGER 36
                ^"Title Ability" STRING "Learned from History"
                ^"Title Ability Effect" STRING "During a mass battle, when you accrue 1 or more momentum points toward the Draw Them In or Seize Victory strategic objective, you accrue that many momentum points plus 1 instead. Additionally, if your action completes that strategic objective, the enemy army receives additional casualties and panic equal to your ranks in Tactics."
                ^"Advancement" LIST OF STRING [
                    "Martial Skills (Skill Group)",
                    "Command (Skill)",
                    "Culture (Skill)",
                    "Government (Skill)",
                    "Rank 1-3 Kata (kata) (Tech Group)",
                    "Rank 1-3 Shūji (shuji) (Tech Group)",
                    "Beseech Akodo's Judgment (ritual)"
                ]
            }
        }

        RULES {
            #L5RFV38rS9tU1vW3xY5zA7b: new_titles "New Titles: The courts of Rokugan like to reward remarkable Imperial citizens with prestigious titles reflecting their glorious deeds and honorable souls. The various positions within a Rokugani army require titles as well. The following new titles follow the rules described on page 305 of the core rulebook."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW DEMEANOR
    # ===========================

    # source (page 142)
    #dbifuv3pkcF22htrb6B8NM ^"Honorable Demeanor" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [#L5R003xY4zA6bC8dE0fG2hI ^"Samurai"]

        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Demeanor" STRING "Honorable"
            ^"Social Skill Check TN Modifiers" STRING "Fire +2, Earth -2"
            ^"Common Way of Unmasking" STRING "Honor's Challenge: The NPC holds to very high standards of behavior and expects others around them to do the same. When they observe breaches of integrity, they are quick to judge what should be the correct action and insist that it be followed."
        }

        RULES {
            #L5RFV40nO1pQ3rS5tU7vW9x: new_demeanor_honorable "New Demeanor: Honorable: The following new demeanor is designed to reflect a personality often found in Lion Clan members and in other samurai who value the tenet of Meiyo—Honor—above all others. Such characters do not hesitate to overcome their fear and act correctly regardless of the consequences. Honorable works in the same manner as the other demeanors on page 310 of the core rulebook."
        }
    }

